        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="1086" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg990"/>

                <head>No. 472.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Maynard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 9,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 225.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 339, of the 29th of
                    August last, in relation to the late homicide at Alexandria, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>Your views as to the true construction of the statutes, as contained in your
                    reply to Mr. N. D. Comanos of the 27th August, are in complete accord with those
                    of the Department and are approved.</p>
                <p>Particular instructions in regard to the conduct of the trial in the case of
                    Mirzan have been given to Mr. Farman, the consul-general, who is now here and
                    about to return to his post, so that it is hoped that you will be relieved from
                    further trouble and responsibility in regard to that unfortunate occurrence.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
